fact WorkItem(id: "WI-495", description: some(value: "Typer half of transitive spec provision (WI-492 follow-up). WI-492 made the EVAL-side dispatch transitive (carrier_param_receiver_for_values → transitive_carrier_for_param in typing.rs), letting the lazy MappedStream/FilteredStream carriers drop their explicit `provides Iterable` + identity `iterator` (their static type is always Stream, so the typer never classifies them). A CONCRETE carrier like List has static type List, so the TYPER's carrier_param_receiver (typing.rs, direct-only) DOES classify it and must compose Element/E from List's provision of Stream — the transitive-binding composition not yet built. Removing List's explicit `provides Iterable[C=List[T], Element=T, E={}]` + `iterator` currently regresses every Iterable.find/map/size/isEmpty/foldLeft on a List to 'undeclared effect: ?_' (the WI-424 effect-row grounding breaks). Fix: make carrier_param_receiver walk transitively like transitive_carrier_for_param AND compose the intermediate spec's element/effect bindings (Iterable.Element ← Stream.T ← List.T; Iterable.E ← Stream.E ← {}) so the grounded row threads. Then delete List's explicit provides Iterable + iterator (see list.anthill comment). Acceptance: remove List's explicit Iterable clause; Iterable ops on a List still type-check pure (no ?_ leak); cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-16T17:30:54Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-495", name: "typing")
